# Contributing

How {{ project_name }} is built and how to change it. Using it: [README.md](README.md).

The rules it follows, each with its reason and its check, live in three places:

- [nuinashco/conventions](https://github.com/nuinashco/conventions/blob/main/GUIDE.md): the rules for every Python
  repo (LAY, ARC, TYP, STY, DOC, ERR, LOG, TST, RDOC, GIT, TOOL). The `conventions` Claude Code plugin carries them
  as skills, with the `conventions-reviewer` and `descriptions-judge` subagents.
- [nuinashco/nuikit](https://github.com/nuinashco/nuikit/blob/main/docs/guide.md): the rules of the library this
  project builds on (FAM, CFG, ERR-1, ERR-2, LOG-1, LOG-3, RUN-1, RUN-2), carried by the `nuikit` plugin's skills.
- [.claude/rules/](.claude/rules/): the rules of [nuinashco/rnd-template](https://github.com/nuinashco/rnd-template),
  which made this project (LAY-4, LAY-7, ENV-1 to ENV-3, TST-5, RUN-3 to RUN-7, TOOL-3); `copier update` refreshes
  them.

