## Import layers

{% if example %}
Dependencies point down: `cli` > `config` > `signals | stats` > `paths`. Siblings joined by `|` never import each
other, and any layer may import `nuikit`.
{% else %}
Dependencies point down: `cli` > `config` > `paths`, and any layer may import `nuikit`.
{% endif %}
The import-linter contract in `pyproject.toml` enforces the order. It is exhaustive, so a new subpackage fails
`make check` until it is placed in `layers`: a domain goes between `config` and `paths`, as a sibling of the domains
it doesn't import or in a layer above them. A standalone subpackage (a proxy, a client) also gets a `forbidden`
contract that keeps it from importing the rest of the package except `paths` (ARC-1).

